{"author":{"affiliation_history":[{"country_code":"US","id":"I97018004","name":"Stanford University","years":[2003,2004,2005,2007,2008,2009,2010,2011,2012,2013,2014,2015,2016,2017,2018,2019,2020,2021,2022,2023,2024,2025,2026]},{"country_code":"US","id":"I55732556","name":"Arizona State University","years":[2025]},{"country_code":"US","id":"I7863295","name":"Villanova University","years":[2025]},{"country_code":"CH","id":"I5124864","name":"\u00c9cole Polytechnique F\u00e9d\u00e9rale de Lausanne","years":[2025]},{"country_code":"US","id":"I36258959","name":"University of California San Diego","years":[2009]},{"country_code":"US","id":"I188538660","name":"University of Colorado Boulder","years":[2009]},{"country_code":"US","id":"I2801919071","name":"University of Illinois System","years":[2009]},{"country_code":"US","id":"I157725225","name":"University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign","years":[2009]},{"country_code":"US","id":"I4210149477","name":"Thornton Tomasetti (United States)","years":[2005]},{"country_code":"US","id":"I205783295","name":"Cornell University","years":[2000,2001,2002,2003]},{"country_code":"US","id":"I2799617873","name":"American Society of Civil Engineers","years":[2001]},{"country_code":"US","id":"I82497590","name":"Auburn University","years":[2001]},{"country_code":"US","id":"I86519309","name":"The University of Texas at Austin","years":[2000,2001]}],"author_id":"A5077663125","ca_plastic_works_count":3,"ca_works_count":3,"citations_by_year":[{"all":253,"plastic":27,"year":2017},{"all":318,"plastic":40,"year":2018},{"all":338,"plastic":35,"year":2019},{"all":382,"plastic":45,"year":2020},{"all":447,"plastic":44,"year":2021},{"all":507,"plastic":50,"year":2022},{"all":500,"plastic":40,"year":2023},{"all":620,"plastic":41,"year":2024},{"all":650,"plastic":24,"year":2025},{"all":490,"plastic":19,"year":2026}],"cited_by_count":5576,"domain_tags":[],"early_career":false,"first_pub_year":1998,"first_year":2013,"h_index":42,"institution_ids":["I97018004"],"last_year":2017,"m_quotient":1.5,"name":"Sarah L. Billington","orcid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3796-587X","plastic_basis":"openalex","plastic_citations":433,"plastic_works_count":3,"primary_affiliations":[{"country_code":"US","id":"I97018004","name":"Stanford University","source":"openalex_last_known"}],"rising_pct":8,"rising_score":-0.0145,"work_count":3,"work_ids":["W2312367806","W2560109694","W2733548549"]},"schema_version":"s3.1","works":[{"abstract":"The need for renewable alternatives to traditional petroleum-derived plastics has driven recent interest in biobased composite materials that are sourced from carbon-neutral feedstocks. Lignin, an abundant plant-derived feedstock, has been a candidate for renewable materials; however, it is often difficult to blend with other biopolymers. In order to improve the miscibility of lignin with other bioplastics, we developed a catalytic and solvent free method for synthesis of a lignin\u2013PLA copolymer. Graft polymerization of lactide onto lignin catalyzed by triazabicyclodecene (TBD) resulted in a lignin- g -poly(lactic acid) copolymer; chain length of the PLA is controlled by varying of the lignin/lactide ratio and preacetylation treatment. End-group analysis reveals high grafting efficiency and preferential grafting on lignin aliphatic hydroxyls over phenolic hydroxyls. The lignin- g -PLA copolymers display a glass transition temperature range from 45 to 85 \u00b0C and multiphase melting behavior. The lignin- g -PLA copolymers are used as dispersion modifiers in PLA-based materials to enhance UV absorption and reduce brittleness without a sacrifice in the modulus of elasticity.","author_count":7,"author_ids":["A5009737401","A5045999960","A5063798984","A5072106065","A5077663125","A5102343129","A5113725499"],"author_institution_ids":["I97018004"],"authors":[{"id":"A5113725499","name":"Yi\u2010Lin Chung"},{"id":"A5072106065","name":"Johan V. Olsson"},{"id":"A5063798984","name":"Russell Jingxian Li"},{"id":"A51023